==English==
{{was wotd|2011|February|21}}

===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:af|summary|-ly<id:adverbial>|text=+|tree=1}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/səˈmɛɹɪli/|/səˈmæɹɪli/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-summarily.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# Of a [[manner]], [[briefly]] or [[concisely]].
#: {{syn|en|unceremoniously}}
#: {{ux|en|They were fired '''summarily''' at a single plant-wide meeting.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1849|author=w:Charles Fitzgerald|title=s:Ordinance enabling transportation of convicts to Western Australia|passage={{...}} and any offender found with firearms in his possession contrary to this Ordinance, shall be deemed to be guilty of a misdemeanor, and being thereof '''summarily''' convicted before any one or more Justice or Justices of the Peace, of being so illegally at large as aforesaid, shall be kept to hard labour on any of the Roads or Public Works of the said colony, for any time not exceeding three calendar months.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=c. 1885-1900|author=w:John Knox Laughton|title=[[s:Rowley, William (1690?-1768) (DNB00)|Rowley, William (1690?-1768)]]|journal=w:Dictionary of National Biography|passage={{...}} but in July 1745 he was '''summarily''' ordered by the secretary of state, the Duke of Newcastle, to return to England.}}
# Of a [[duration]], over a short [[period of time]], [[briefly]].
#: {{syn|en|ephemerally|fleetingly|transiently|see also [[Thesaurus:temporarily]]}}
#: {{ux|en|He covered the topic '''summarily''' in an answer to a question.}}
#* {{RQ:Heller Catch-22|The Soldier in White|168|They didn't get shot to death in hold-ups, strangled to death in rapes, stabbed to death in saloons, bludgeoned to death with axes by parents or children or die '''summarily''' by some other act of God.}}

